# SQLAlchemy 2.x — Best Practices

<!-- cs: Doporučené postupy pro SQLAlchemy 2.x -->

Use **SQLAlchemy 2.x style exclusively** — `DeclarativeBase`, `Mapped`, `mapped_column`.
Legacy `declarative_base()` and `session.query()` are **prohibited**.
<!-- cs: Používej výhradně SQLAlchemy 2.x styl — DeclarativeBase, Mapped, mapped_column.
     Starý declarative_base() a session.query() jsou zakázány. -->

## Model Definition

<!-- cs: Definice modelů -->

```python
# ✅ SQLAlchemy 2.x + PostgreSQL conventions (UUID PK, TIMESTAMPTZ)
from uuid import UUID
from datetime import datetime
from sqlalchemy import String, ForeignKey, text
from sqlalchemy.dialects.postgresql import UUID as PGUUID, JSONB
from sqlalchemy.orm import DeclarativeBase, Mapped, mapped_column, relationship

class Base(DeclarativeBase):
    pass

class TimestampMixin:
    """Add created_at / updated_at to any model."""
    created_at: Mapped[datetime] = mapped_column(
        server_default=text("NOW()"), nullable=False
    )
    updated_at: Mapped[datetime | None] = mapped_column(onupdate=text("NOW()"))

class Document(Base, TimestampMixin):
    __tablename__ = "documents"

    id: Mapped[UUID] = mapped_column(
        PGUUID(as_uuid=True), primary_key=True, server_default=text("gen_random_uuid()")
    )
    source_id: Mapped[str] = mapped_column(String, nullable=False, unique=True)
    metadata_: Mapped[dict | None] = mapped_column("metadata", JSONB)

    versions: Mapped[list["DocumentVersion"]] = relationship(
        back_populates="document", cascade="all, delete-orphan"
    )
```

## Async Session (FastAPI / asyncio)

<!-- cs: Async session (FastAPI / asyncio) -->

```python
# session.py
from sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import AsyncSession, async_sessionmaker, create_async_engine

engine = create_async_engine(settings.DATABASE_URL, pool_pre_ping=True)
AsyncSessionFactory = async_sessionmaker(engine, expire_on_commit=False)

async def get_session() -> AsyncGenerator[AsyncSession, None]:
    async with AsyncSessionFactory() as session:
        yield session

# FastAPI dependency
from typing import Annotated
from fastapi import Depends
SessionDep = Annotated[AsyncSession, Depends(get_session)]
```

- `expire_on_commit=False` — objects remain accessible after commit (important in FastAPI).
  <!-- cs: expire_on_commit=False — objekty zůstávají přístupné po commitu (důležité ve FastAPI). -->
- Always `yield` inside `async with` — ensures rollback on unhandled exceptions.
  <!-- cs: Vždy yield uvnitř async with — zajišťuje rollback při neošetřené výjimce. -->

## Querying — 2.x Style

<!-- cs: Dotazy — 2.x styl -->

```python
from sqlalchemy import select

# ✅ select() + session.scalar() / scalars()
async def get_by_source_id(session: AsyncSession, source_id: str) -> Document | None:
    stmt = select(Document).where(Document.source_id == source_id)
    return await session.scalar(stmt)

# ✅ Multiple results
async def list_active(session: AsyncSession) -> list[Document]:
    stmt = select(Document).where(Document.is_active == True).order_by(Document.created_at)
    result = await session.scalars(stmt)
    return list(result.all())
```

```python
# ❌ Legacy — prohibited
session.query(Document).filter(Document.source_id == source_id).first()
```

## Eager Loading — Avoid N+1

<!-- cs: Eager loading — zamezení N+1 -->

```python
from sqlalchemy.orm import selectinload, joinedload

# ✅ selectinload — preferred for collections (separate IN query)
stmt = select(Document).options(selectinload(Document.versions))

# ✅ joinedload — preferred for single objects (JOIN)
stmt = select(DocumentVersion).options(joinedload(DocumentVersion.document))

# ❌ Never access a relationship in a loop without eager loading
for doc in docs:
    print(doc.versions)  # N+1 queries — prohibited
```

## Repository Pattern with Async

<!-- cs: Repository pattern s async -->

```python
# Pattern: Repository
class DocumentRepository:
    def __init__(self, session: AsyncSession) -> None:
        self._session = session

    async def get(self, source_id: str) -> Document | None:
        stmt = select(Document).where(Document.source_id == source_id)
        return await self._session.scalar(stmt)

    async def save(self, doc: Document) -> Document:
        self._session.add(doc)
        await self._session.flush()  # assign PK without committing
        await self._session.refresh(doc)
        return doc
```

- `flush()` assigns auto-generated PKs without committing the transaction.
  <!-- cs: flush() přiřadí auto-generované PK bez commitu transakce. -->
- Commit belongs to the **caller** (the service layer), not the repository.
  <!-- cs: Commit patří volajícímu (service layer), ne repository. -->

## Alembic — Autogenerate with Async Engine

<!-- cs: Alembic — autogenerate s async engine -->

```python
# alembic/env.py — async pattern
from sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import create_async_engine
from logging.config import fileConfig
from alembic import context
from src.db.models import Base  # import your Base so metadata is populated

target_metadata = Base.metadata

def run_migrations_online() -> None:
    connectable = create_async_engine(config.get_main_option("sqlalchemy.url"))

    async def run() -> None:
        async with connectable.connect() as connection:
            await connection.run_sync(
                context.configure,
                connection=connection,
                target_metadata=target_metadata,
            )
            async with context.begin_transaction():
                await connection.run_sync(context.run_migrations)

    import asyncio
    asyncio.run(run())
```

```bash
# Generate migration from model changes
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add source_id index to documents"

# Apply
alembic upgrade head

# Rollback one step
alembic downgrade -1
```

- Always **review autogenerated migrations** before applying — `--autogenerate` misses some ops.
  <!-- cs: Vždy kontroluj autogenerované migrace před aplikací — --autogenerate některé operace přehlédne. -->
- Every migration must have a working `downgrade()`. See `13-sql-postgresql.mdc` for SQL conventions.
  <!-- cs: Každá migrace musí mít funkční downgrade(). SQL konvence viz 13-sql-postgresql.mdc. -->
